WEBVTT

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.240
Emiyan!

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.410
When you're through with that,
help me out with this, okay?

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.700
You got it!

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.960
I'm gonna bring the car to the back of the shop,

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.300
so could you carry these out?

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.340
They're pretty heavy, so be careful!

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.850
<i>Today I happened to stop by my part-time job,</i>

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.020
<i>and before I knew it, I found myself enlisted to help out.</i>

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.730
<i>This is Neko.</i>

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.570
<i>She's the daughter of the owner
of the liquor store, "Copenhagen."</i>

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:18.950
Let's go!

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.700
<i>She graduated from Homurahara Academy ahead of me,</i>

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.120
<i>and she was one of Fuji-nee's classmates.</i>

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.170
<i>She looks out for me in all kinds of ways.</i>

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.760
Hey, my bad, Emiyan... Making you help out like this...

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.140
Ryudou Temple's our last stop, okay?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.930
Hey, don't mention it.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.270
It's just that there's more than usual.
I can probably manage on my own.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.480
Um, the amount isn't the only problem.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.570
Pretty inconvenient for this day and age, huh?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.530
You'd better not talk. It's dangerous!

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.370
Now watch your step!

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.790
Shoot!

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.970
<i>Sure he'd be here. Of course.</i>

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.270
Well, hello, Neko.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.310
Shirou.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.270
Reikan.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.230
Hey, Rei! Here we are.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.570
What's wrong?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.330
I've hardly ever been this far inside a temple.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.910
There's actually a lot of people around, huh?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:53.540
True. It probably seems pretty deserted to an outsider.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.170
But temples are communities, too.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:01.510
Sure, it would be way too lonely
in a place like this even for a monk.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.100
Neko, I don't appreciate the term "a place like this."

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.100
Lonely, huh?

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.520
All right! That's all she wrote!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.560
I really owe you one!

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.110
I'll be glad to help out anytime. This was nothing.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.690
Good work, you two!

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.070
Are these spring greens?

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.120
And a lot of other stuff, too.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.950
Yeah. We received quite a lot, you see.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.620
I thought I'd ask whoever's on cooking
duty to make tempura or maybe boil them.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:38.710
You know, I bet these would taste good in a sandwich.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.130
And it would be a quick meal, too.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.470
A sandwich?

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.140
You boil the greens,

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:51.520
slather crispy-fried bacon and eggs
with a whole grain mustard sauce,

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.440
and stick them between bread.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:56.980
Emiyan?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.570
Shirou...

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:04.780
I, too, am somewhat intrigued by the
notion of this "sandwich" you speak of.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:09.160
Um, I guess that means that
you'd like to try it right now.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.000
Feel free to use the kitchen area as you like!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:17.960
If you need anything,
I'll be happy to run out and get it, okay?

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:28.260
The Ryudou Temple kitchen is
better-equipped than I thought it would be.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.270
The fact that some of the utensils look brand-new,

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.310
by any chance, could this mean...

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.480
<i>I shall prepare all of your meals, Mr. Souichirou.</i>

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.780
So she's been cooking, huh?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.160
I'm gonna borrow your stuff, okay?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.830
Spring has come again this year, huh?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.000
After our high school graduation,

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.590
the three of us came here to
Ryudou Temple, remember?

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:09.100
Fujimura made such a commotion
that she got yelled at by your dad.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:13.770
Hey, I know!

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.270
Why don't we invite Fujimura over to join us for lunch?

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.270
She's got club activities today,
so she's at work, according to Shirou.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:24.240
Is that right?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.700
I guess we all grew up and became adults, huh?

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.960
Blend some Japanese mustard and butter together

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.210
to make a mustard butter spread for the bread.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:45.050
Mix mayonnaise, whole grain mustard,
honey and coarse ground pepper together

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.880
to make your sandwich sauce.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.640
Add a dash of salt to some boiling water.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.770
Add the spring greens, stalk-first,
since the stalks take longer to cook,

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.230
and boil them for a minute or two.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.560
After boiling, immerse them in ice water,

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.730
then make sure they're fully drained.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.490
Salt the eggs beforehand,

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.860
then scramble them.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.620
Pour a little extra oil to fry the bacon in,

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.870
and let them get crispy on low to medium heat.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.290
When they're done, blot them with
paper towels to remove the excess oil.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.090
Spread the mustard butter on one side of the bread,

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.800
and layer the filling on top of it.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.560
When you're done, don't cut them yet.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.100
Instead, cover the bread with
plastic wrap, so it won't dry out.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.320
Weigh them down lightly with
something flat for five to ten minutes

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.110
to blend all the ingredients together.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.500
Emiyan, you're amazing!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.210
Looks so yummy!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.670
I did hear from Issei what a great cook you are!

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.130
Neko!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.880
Why don't we partake of this meal?

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.300
Let's dig in!

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:16.390
Now, then,

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.810
what do you want...

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.020
Saber's Master?

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.400
Um...

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.520
So Caster's not around right now, huh?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.690
Your business is with Caster, then?

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.070
Unfortunately, she's gone off with her Master.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.280
Is that what you came to ask?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.120
Uh, no.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:43.080
I made sandwiches and was
wondering if you'd like to have some.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.380
Well, well...

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:48.670
You may set them down there.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.550
I shall partake.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.590
Gotcha!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.680
All right, I'll come pick up the plate later.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.200
This is...

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.750
...not bad at all.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:31.210
So spring greens can be eaten this way, as well.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:36.180
You can also use them in pasta,
and they're good in croquettes, too.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:40.560
Hey, what do you think about adding this to our menu?

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.930
Made by you, of course, Emiyan!

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.350
I've returned home!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.110
Is that you, Emiya?

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.110
Yeah.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.400
Hey, so you're back, Issei?

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:58.820
We just sat down to have some
of Shirou's homemade sandwiches.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.490
Better dig in right away, or there won't be any left!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:02.910
What did you say?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.160
Reikan!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.620
That's totally unfair!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.500
There's more, so let me bring them over.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.140
Not here, huh?

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:19.130
So you're not inclined to make them?

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.350
Those things called "sandwiches."

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.100
Where did that come from?
